    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS). The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented a daily owner-creation limit on `POST /api/owners` that rejects with **429 Too Many Requests** once 100 or more owners have been created today (by `registrationDate`), following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions (mirroring the existing `EnsureCityCapacity` rule).\n\n**New files:**\n- `EnsureDailyLimit.java` \u2014 function step that counts existing owners whose `registrationDate` equals `LocalDate.now()` and throws `DailyLimitExceededException` at 100+.\n- `DailyLimitExceededException.java` \u2014 checked exception (so it appears in the `throws` clause).\n- `DailyLimitExceededExceptionHandler.java` \u2014 responds `429` with a `ProblemDetail` body.\n- `...escalation/...DailyLimitExceededException.yml` \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n\n**Modified:**\n- `owners.POST.yml` \u2014 inserted the `ensureDailyLimit` step (under `transaction` governance) between `ensureCityCapacity` and `build`, so the check runs on existing owners before the new one is saved.\n\nThe count is taken over existing owners only (the new owner isn't saved yet), so the 101st create in a day is the one rejected \u2014 exactly what `AcceptanceTest.coreRejectsOverDailyLimit` asserts.",
